#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:1
msgid "Lockable HTTP Tarball Protocol"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:3
msgid ""
"Tarball flakes can be served as regular tarballs via HTTP or the file system "
"(for `file://` URLs). Unless the server implements the Lockable HTTP Tarball "
"protocol, it is the responsibility of the user to make sure that the URL "
"always produces the same tarball contents."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:8
msgid ""
"An HTTP server can return an \"immutable\" HTTP URL appropriate for lock "
"files. This allows users to specify a tarball flake input in `flake.nix` "
"that requests the latest version of a flake (e.g. `https://example.org/hello/"
"latest.tar.gz`), while `flake.lock` will record a URL whose contents will "
"not change (e.g. `https://example.org/hello/<revision>.tar.gz`). To do so, "
"the server must return an [HTTP `Link` header](https://developer.mozilla.org/"
"en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Headers/Link) with the `rel` attribute set to "
"`immutable`, as follows:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:17
msgid ""
"```\n"
"Link: <flakeref>; rel=\"immutable\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:21
msgid "(Note the required `<` and `>` characters around _flakeref_.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:23
msgid ""
"_flakeref_ must be a tarball flakeref. It can contain the tarball flake "
"attributes `narHash`, `rev`, `revCount` and `lastModified`. If `narHash` is "
"included, its value must be the \\[NAR hash\\]\\[Nix Archive\\] of the "
"unpacked tarball (as computed via `nix hash path`). Nix checks the contents "
"of the returned tarball against the `narHash` attribute. The `rev` and "
"`revCount` attributes are useful when the tarball flake is a mirror of a "
"fetcher type that has those attributes, such as Git or GitHub. They are not "
"checked by Nix."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:32
msgid ""
"```\n"
"Link: <https://example.org/hello/442793d9ec0584f6a6e82fa253850c8085bb150a."
"tar.gz\n"
"  ?rev=442793d9ec0584f6a6e82fa253850c8085bb150a\n"
"  &revCount=835\n"
"  &narHash=sha256-GUm8Uh/U74zFCwkvt9Mri4DSM%2BmHj3tYhXUkYpiv31M%3D>; "
"rel=\"immutable\"\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:39
msgid ""
"(The linebreaks in this example are for clarity and must not be included in "
"the actual response.)"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:41
msgid ""
"For tarball flakes, the value of the `lastModified` flake attribute is "
"defined as the timestamp of the newest file inside the tarball."
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:44
msgid "Gitea and Forgejo support"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:46
msgid ""
"This protocol is supported by Gitea since v1.22.1 and by Forgejo since "
"v7.0.4/v8.0.0 and can be used with the following flake URL schema:"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:48
msgid ""
"```\n"
"https://<domain name>/<owner>/<repo>/archive/<reference or revision>.tar.gz\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:52
msgid "**Example**"
msgstr ""

#: source/protocols/tarball-fetcher.md:55
msgid ""
"```nix\n"
"# flake.nix\n"
"{\n"
"   inputs = {\n"
"     foo.url = \"https://gitea.example.org/some-person/some-flake/archive/"
"main.tar.gz\";\n"
"     bar.url = \"https://gitea.example.org/some-other-person/other-flake/"
"archive/442793d9ec0584f6a6e82fa253850c8085bb150a.tar.gz\";\n"
"     qux = {\n"
"       url = \"https://forgejo.example.org/another-person/some-non-flake-"
"repo/archive/development.tar.gz\";\n"
"       flake = false;\n"
"     };\n"
"   };\n"
"   outputs = { foo, bar, qux }: { /* ... */ };\n"
"}\n"
"```"
msgstr ""
